%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::has_jacobian "

Return Jacobian of all input elements with respect to all output elements.

Override has_jacobian() to return true and get_jacobian() to return a
Function with inputs [all nominal inputs, all nominal outputs] and one
output per (output, input) pair, each the dense or sparse Jacobian block of
that output with respect to that input (row-major over the pairs). Use the
``inames``, ``onames`` and ``opts`` passed in: they carry the expected names
and the \"derivative_of\" option. The returned Function may be an SX/MX
Function (then higher derivatives are exact) or another Callback (keep a
reference to it).



::

  >>> class F43(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def get_sparsity_in(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(4, 1)
  ...   def get_sparsity_out(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(3, 1)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     a, b, c, d = vertsplit(arg[0])
  ...     return [vertcat(sin(c)*d+d**2, 2*a+c, b**2+5*c)]
  ...   def has_jacobian(self): return True
  ...   def get_jacobian(self, name, inames, onames, opts):
  ...     print(name, inames, onames)
  ...     x = SX.sym(\"x\", 4)
  ...     y = SX.sym(\"y\", Sparsity(3, 1))
  ...     a, b, c, d = vertsplit(x)
  ...     J = blockcat([[0, 0, d*cos(c), sin(c)+2*d], [2, 0, 1, 0], [0, 2*b, 5, 0]])
  ...     return Function(name, [x, y], [J], inames, onames, opts)
  >>> f = F43(\"f\")
  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\", 4)
  >>> J = Function(\"J\", [x], [jacobian(f(x), x)])
  jac_f ['i0', 'out_o0'] ['jac_o0_i0']
  >>> J([1, 2, 0, 3])
  DM(
  [[0, 0, 3, 6],
   [2, 0, 1, 0],
   [0, 4, 5, 0]])
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_oh

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L725
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.cpp#L100-L102
";

