%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::has_forward "

Return function that calculates forward derivatives.

Override has_forward(nfwd) to return true for the numbers of directions you
support (nfwd==1 is enough; CasADi then loops) and get_forward() to return a
Function with inputs [nominal inputs, nominal outputs, one forward seed per
input] and one forward sensitivity per output. For nfwd>1 the seeds and
sensitivities are horizontally stacked (n-by-nfwd*m). forward(nfwd) on the
Function caches the result.



::

  >>> class Sq(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[0]**2]
  ...   def has_forward(self, nfwd): return nfwd == 1
  ...   def get_forward(self, nfwd, name, inames, onames, opts):
  ...     print(nfwd, name, inames, onames)
  ...     x, y, xd = SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"y\", Sparsity(1, 1)), SX.sym(\"xd\")
  ...     return Function(name, [x, y, xd], [2*x*xd], inames, onames, opts)
  >>> f = Sq(\"f\")
  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> J = Function(\"J\", [x], [jacobian(f(x), x)])
  1 fwd1_f ['i0', 'out_o0', 'fwd_i0'] ['fwd_o0']
  >>> J(3)
  DM(6)
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_oi

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L788
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.cpp#L120-L122
";

