%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::size1_in "

Get the shape of an input: rows, columns or both.

size1_in is the number of rows, size2_in the number of columns and size_in
the pair (rows, columns). The input is selected by index or by name; an
unknown name raises an error listing the available names, an index out of
range raises an error.



::

  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [SX.sym(\"A\", 2, 3), SX.sym(\"b\", 2)], [SX(0)], [\"A\", \"b\"], [\"c\"])
  >>> f.size_in(0), f.size1_in(\"A\"), f.size2_in(\"A\")
  ((2, 3), 2, 3)
  >>> f.size_in(\"b\")
  (2, 1)
  >>> try:
  ...   f.size_in(\"nope\")
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"Available names are: [A, b]\" in str(e))
