%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::convert_in "

Convert between a list and a dict of inputs or outputs.

convert_in turns a list of n_in() values into a dict keyed by input name,
and a dict into a list where absent inputs get default_in. convert_out does
the same for outputs; absent outputs become nan. An unknown key or a list of
the wrong length raises an error. Values are passed through unchanged (no
shape or sparsity check), for any of DM, SX and MX. Useful to prepare
arguments for call or generate_in.



::

  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"y\")], [SX(0), SX(1)], [\"x\", \"y\"], [\"a\", \"b\"])
  >>> f.convert_in([1, 2])
  {'x': DM(1), 'y': DM(2)}
  >>> f.convert_in({\"y\": 2})
  [DM(0), DM(2)]
  >>> f.convert_out({\"b\": 5})
  [DM(nan), DM(5)]
  >>> try:
  ...   f.convert_in({\"z\": 1})
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print('could not find entry \"z\"' in str(e))
  True
  





See also: call, default_in, nz_from_in

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1x7

