%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::eval "

Evaluate numerically.

The method a subclass must implement. Receives one DM per input (with the
sparsity of get_sparsity_in) and must return a list with one entry per
output; each entry is converted to a DM and must match the shape of
get_sparsity_out, otherwise the call raises an error. Exceptions raised
inside propagate to the caller. The default implementation raises an error.

This signature is not thread-safe. For guaranteed thread-safety, use
eval_buffer.



Parameters:
    arg: Input values



Returns:
    Output values



::

  >>> class Scale(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def get_n_in(self): return 2
  ...   def get_sparsity_in(self, i):
  ...     return Sparsity.dense(2, 1) if i == 0 else Sparsity.dense(1, 1)
  ...   def get_sparsity_out(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(2, 1)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[0]*arg[1]]
  >>> f = Scale(\"f\")
  >>> f([1, 2], 3)
  DM([3, 6])
  >>> class Bad(Scale):
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[1]]
  >>> try:
  ...   Bad(\"b\")([1, 2], 3)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Shape mismatch\" in str(e))
  True
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_o8

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L409
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.cpp#L60-L62
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::eval_buffer "

A copy-free low level interface.

Alternative to eval() that works on the raw nonzero buffers, avoiding DM
allocation. Override has_eval_buffer() to return true to activate it. In
Python the method receives two tuples of memoryview objects (inputs and
outputs), each holding only the structural nonzeros of the corresponding
input or output in column-major order; write the result into the output
buffers and return 0.



::

  >>> class Sq(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def get_sparsity_in(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(3, 1)
  ...   def get_sparsity_out(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(3, 1)
  ...   def has_eval_buffer(self): return True
  ...   def eval_buffer(self, arg, res):
  ...     a = np.frombuffer(arg[0], dtype=np.float64)
  ...     r = np.frombuffer(res[0], dtype=np.float64)
  ...     r[:] = a**2
  ...     return 0
  >>> f = Sq(\"f\")
  >>> f([1, 2, 3])
  DM([1, 4, 9])
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_o9

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L438
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.cpp#L53-L56
";

