%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::get_sparsity_in "

Get the sparsity of an input.

Called during construct() for i in 0..n_in-1. Default: scalar (1-by-1
dense). Inputs are padded or projected to this pattern when the Function is
called.



::

  >>> class Trace(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, n, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.n = n
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def get_sparsity_in(self, i): return Sparsity.diag(self.n)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [sum1(diag(arg[0]))]
  >>> f = Trace(\"f\", 3)
  >>> f.sparsity_in(0), f(DM.ones(3, 3))
