%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::uses_output "

Do the derivative functions need nondifferentiated outputs?

Derivative functions obtained from get_jacobian/get_forward/get_reverse
receive the nominal outputs as extra inputs. When this returns false
(default) those inputs are passed as empty (all-zero sparsity) placeholders;
return true to receive the actual output values, e.g. to reuse them in the
derivative computation.



::

  >>> class Sq(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[0]**2]
  ...   def has_jacobian(self): return True
  ...   def get_jacobian(self, name, inames, onames, opts):
  ...     x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  ...     y = SX.sym(\"y\", self.sparsity_out(0) if self.uses_output() else Sparsity(1, 1))
  ...     return Function(name, [x, y], [2*x], inames, onames, opts)
  >>> class SqU(Sq):
  ...   def uses_output(self): return True
  >>> Sq(\"f\").jacobian().sparsity_in(1), SqU(\"f\").jacobian().sparsity_in(1)
  (Sparsity(1x1,0nz), Sparsity(1x1))
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_og

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L637
