%feature("docstring") casadi::Callback::default_in "

Get the value used for input ``ind`` when a call by name omits it.

When calling with a dict (or keyword arguments), every input that is not
given is filled with this scalar, broadcast to the input shape. For
functions built from expressions it is 0 unless option \"default_in\" was
set at construction. Solvers define their own: nlpsol uses -inf for lbx and
lbg, inf for ubx and ubg, 0 for the rest.



