%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::x "

Differential states.

Names of the variables of category ``x``, in category order. Equivalent to
``all(\"x\")``. A continuous variable becomes a differential state once its
time derivative is given a defining equation with ``eq``; it is an algebraic
variable ``z`` before that.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\")
  >>> dae.x(), dae.z()
  ([], ['x', 'y'])
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -y)
  >>> dae.x(), dae.z(), dae.nx()
  (['x'], ['y'], 1)
  





See also: z, q, nx, all, inputs

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_5f

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L309
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L309-L309
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::y "

Outputs.

Names of the variables with causality ``\"output\"``, in category order.
Equivalent to ``all(\"y\")``. Outputs are also members of another category
(``x``, ``w``, ``z``, ...); ``outputs(\"y\")`` gives their expressions.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\", \"output\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\", \"output\")
  >>> w = dae.add(\"w\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w)
  >>> dae.eq(w, x**2)
  >>> dae.eq(y, 2*x)
  >>> dae.y(), dae.x(), dae.w()
  (['x', 'y'], ['x'], ['der(x)', 'w', 'y'])
  >>> dae.outputs(\"y\")
  [MX(x), MX(y)]
  >>> dae.set_causality(\"y\", \"local\")
  >>> dae.y(), dae.ny()
  (['x'], 1)
  





See also: set_causality, set_all, ny, outputs

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2fu

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L358
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L358-L358
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::z "

Algebraic variables.

Names of the variables of category ``z``, in category order. Equivalent to
``all(\"z\")``. Every continuous ``local`` or ``output`` variable starts in
this category and leaves it when it gets a defining equation (``w``) or an
equation for its derivative (``x``).



See also: x, w, nz, eq

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2fv

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L369
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L369-L369
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::q "

Quadrature states.

Names of the variables of category ``q``: differential states that do not
appear in any right-hand side. Equivalent to ``all(\"q\")``. A state is only
placed here by ``set_category(name, \"q\")`` or automatically with the
constructor option ``\"detect_quad\"``.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> q = dae.add(\"q\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(q), x**2)
  >>> dae.x(), dae.q()
  (['x', 'q'], [])
  >>> dae.set_category(\"q\", \"q\")
  >>> dae.x(), dae.q(), dae.outputs(\"quad\")
  (['x'], ['q'], [MX(sq(x))])
  





See also: set_category, x, nq

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2fw

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L408
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L408-L408
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::inputs "

Input expressions for a specific category.

The symbolic expressions of the variables of an input category, in category
order.



Parameters:
    cat: One of ``\"t\"``, ``\"c\"``, ``\"p\"``, ``\"d\"``, ``\"w\"``, ``\"u\"``, ``\"x\"``, ``\"z\"``, ``\"q\"``; an output category such as ``\"ode\"`` is an error



Returns:
    List of (column vector) expressions, one per variable; empty when the category is empty



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> z = dae.add(\"z\")
  >>> u = dae.add(\"u\", \"input\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x + z*u)
  >>> dae.eq(0, x - 2*z)
  >>> dae.inputs(\"x\"), dae.inputs(\"z\"), dae.inputs(\"u\"), dae.inputs(\"p\")
  ([MX(x)], [MX(z)], [MX(u)], [])
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.inputs(\"ode\")
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"not an input category\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: outputs, var, all

