%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::eq "

Add a simple equation.

Adds the equation ``lhs == rhs`` and reclassifies variables accordingly:



- ``lhs`` is the derivative of a state (``der(x)``): the equation becomes the ODE of ``x``, which moves from ``z`` to ``x``; ``der(x)`` becomes a dependent variable ``w``
- ``lhs`` is a variable of category ``z``: the equation is its binding equation and the variable moves to ``w``; it must not have a binding equation already
- ``lhs`` is a concatenation of such variables: split into one equation per component
- ``lhs`` is anything else, typically ``0``: an implicit (algebraic) equation ``0 == lhs - rhs`` is added to ``outputs(\"alg\")``; a second equation for a variable that already has a binding equation is treated this way too



A derivative ``der(x)`` that appears in ``rhs`` before it was defined is
replaced by a new algebraic variable ``der_x`` with the trivial ODE ``der(x)
== der_x``, keeping the DAE semi-explicit. Scalar sides are broadcast to the
length of the other side; sparse sides are densified. Variables appearing in
``rhs`` are marked as used, so a quadrature state ``q`` referenced there
becomes a regular state ``x``.



Parameters:
    lhs: Column vector expression; a parameter, constant or state as left-hand side is an error
    rhs: Column vector expression in model variables only; dimensions must match after broadcasting
    opts: Must be empty



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\")
  >>> z = dae.add(\"z\")
  >>> w = dae.add(\"w\")
  >>> dae.x(), dae.z(), dae.w()
  ([], ['x', 'y', 'z', 'w'], [])
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x + z)
  >>> dae.x(), dae.z(), dae.w()
  (['x'], ['y', 'z', 'w'], ['der(x)'])
  >>> dae.eq(0, x - 2*z)
  >>> dae.z(), dae.outputs(\"alg\")
  (['y', 'z', 'w'], [MX((-(x-(2.*z))))])
  >>> dae.eq(w, x*z)
  >>> dae.w(), dae.wdef()
  (['der(x)', 'w'], [MX((z-x)), MX((x*z))])
  >>> dae.eq(vertcat(dae.der(y), w), vertcat(w, 1))
  >>> dae.x(), dae.outputs(\"ode\"), dae.outputs(\"alg\")
  (['x', 'y'], [MX((z-x)), MX(w)], [MX((-(x-(2.*z)))), MX((-(w-1)))])
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.eq(x, 1)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Cannot handle left-hand-side\" in str(e))
  True
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.eq(vertcat(dae.der(x), dae.der(y)), vertcat(1, 2, 3))
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Mismatched dimensions\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: der, when, set_init, add

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2kt

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1066
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L385-L391
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::when "

Add when equations.

Adds an event: whenever the zero-crossing function of ``cond`` becomes
negative, the assignments in ``eqs`` are executed. The condition must be a
strict inequality ``a < b`` (or ``a > b``); it is stored as the zero-
crossing function ``a - b`` in ``outputs(\"zero\")``. The event transition
can be obtained with ``transition``.



Parameters:
    cond: Strict inequality between model expressions; ``<=`` or any other expression is an error
    eqs: Names returned by ``reinit`` or ``assign``; may be empty
    opts: Must be empty



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"ball\")
  >>> h = dae.add(\"h\", dict(start=5))
  >>> v = dae.add(\"v\", dict(start=0))
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(h), v)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(v), -9.81)
  >>> dae.when(h < 0, [dae.reinit(\"v\", -0.8*v)])
  >>> dae.nzero(), dae.outputs(\"zero\")
  (1, [MX(h)])
  >>> T = dae.transition()
  >>> T
  Function(ball_transition:(index[],t[0],x[2],z[0],p[0],u[0])->(post_x[2],post_z[0]) MXFunction)
  >>> T(0, 0, [-0.1, -3], [], [], [])
  (DM([-0.1, 2.4]), DM(0x1))
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.when(h <= 0, [])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Only strict inequality\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: reinit, assign, transition, nzero

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ku

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1122
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L393-L399
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::assign "

Assignment inside a when-equation or if-else equation.

Creates a helper variable holding the expression ``val`` assigned to the
variable ``name`` when the event fires, and returns the helper's name for
use in ``when``. Intended for discrete-valued variables; ``reinit`` is the
counterpart for continuous states.



Parameters:
    name: Model variable that receives the value
    val: Expression in model variables



Returns:
    Name of the created assignment variable, e.g. ``__assign__b__``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\", dict(start=0))
  >>> b = dae.add(\"b\", dict(type=\"Boolean\", start=False))
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), 1)
  >>> dae.assign(\"b\", True)
  '__assign__b__'
  >>> dae.when(x > 1, [dae.assign(\"b\", True)])
  >>> dae.disp(True)
  nt = 0, nx = 2, nz = 0, nq = 0, ny = 0, np = 0, nc = 0, nd = 0, nw = 1, nu = 0
  Model variables:
    x = [x, b]
    w = [der(x)]
  List of dependent variables (w):
    der(x) := 1
  Time derivatives of differential states (x):
    x: der(x)
    b: 0
  When equations:
    when (1-x) < 0 :
      b := 1
  





See also: when, reinit

