%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::reinit "

Reinitialize a state inside when-equations.

Creates a helper variable holding the new value ``val`` of the state
``name`` after the event, and returns the helper's name for use in ``when``.
Use ``pre(v)`` for the value before the event (currently an identity
mapping).



Parameters:
    name: Model variable that is reinitialized
    val: Expression in model variables



Returns:
    Name of the created variable, e.g. ``__reinit__v__0``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"ball\")
  >>> h = dae.add(\"h\", dict(start=5))
  >>> v = dae.add(\"v\", dict(start=0))
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(h), v)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(v), -9.81)
  >>> r = dae.reinit(\"v\", -0.8*v)
  >>> r, dae.category(r)
  ('__reinit__v__0', 'calculated')
  >>> dae.when(h < 0, [r])
  >>> dae.nzero()
  1
  





See also: when, assign, pre

