%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::reorder "

Reorder variables in a category.

Replaces the ordering of a category by ``v``, which must be a permutation of
the current members: a missing or extra name is an error. The ordering
determines the order of the entries in the vectors used by ``create`` (e.g.
of ``x`` and ``ode``).



Parameters:
    cat: Category name, e.g. ``\"x\"``
    v: All current members of the category, in the new order



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -y)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(y), x)
  >>> dae.x(), dae.outputs(\"ode\")
  (['x', 'y'], [MX((-y)), MX(x)])
  >>> dae.reorder(\"x\", [\"y\", \"x\"])
  >>> dae.x(), dae.outputs(\"ode\")
  (['y', 'x'], [MX(x), MX((-y))])
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.reorder(\"x\", [\"y\"])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"1 elements provided for 2 components\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: set_all, all

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2kz

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1337
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L333-L339
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::set_all "

Set all variables within a a category.

Makes ``name`` the complete, ordered content of category ``v``, moving
variables in and out as needed:



- ``\"y\"``: the listed variables get causality ``\"output\"``, all other outputs become ``\"local\"``
- ``\"u\"``, ``\"p\"``, ``\"c\"``: the listed variables are moved into the category with ``set_category``; members not listed become constants ``c`` (for ``\"u\"`` and ``\"p\"``)
- ``\"x\"``, ``\"q\"``: the listed states are moved in; members not listed lose their category (they must not appear in any right-hand side)



Other categories and duplicate names are an error. Names not permitted in
the category raise the error of ``set_category``.



Parameters:
    v: Category name
    name: Variables that should form the category, in order



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> u1 = dae.add(\"u1\", \"input\")
  >>> p1 = dae.add(\"p1\", \"parameter\", \"tunable\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x + u1*p1)
  >>> dae.set_all(\"u\", [\"p1\", \"u1\"])
  >>> dae.u(), dae.p(), dae.c()
  (['p1', 'u1'], [], [])
  >>> dae.set_all(\"p\", [\"u1\"])
  >>> dae.u(), dae.p(), dae.c()
  (['p1'], ['u1'], [])
  >>> dae.set_all(\"y\", [\"x\"])
  >>> dae.y(), dae.causality(\"x\")
  (['x'], 'output')
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.set_all(\"x\", [\"x\", \"x\"])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Duplicate names\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: reorder, set_category, set_causality

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2l0

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1405
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L281-L331
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::dependent_fun "

Construct a function for evaluating dependent parameters.

Builds a Function that calculates the dependent parameters ``d`` and/or
dependent variables ``w`` from their binding equations, substituting the
interdependencies out, with the given categories as inputs.



Parameters:
    fname: Function name
    s_in: Input categories; a category that is also an output is an error, and every variable the definitions depend on must be covered
    s_out: ``\"d\"``, ``\"w\"`` or both; anything else is an error



Returns:
    Function with one (concatenated) output per entry of ``s_out``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> w1 = dae.add(\"w1\")
  >>> w2 = dae.add(\"w2\")
  >>> p = dae.add(\"p\", \"parameter\", \"tunable\")
  >>> dae.eq(w1, 2*x)
  >>> dae.eq(w2, w1**2 + p)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w2)
  >>> f = dae.dependent_fun(\"f\", [\"x\", \"p\"], [\"w\"])
  >>> f
  Function(f:(x,p)->(w[3]) MXFunction)
  >>> f(1, 3)
  DM([2, 7, -7])
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.dependent_fun(\"f\", [\"x\", \"w\"], [\"w\"])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"cannot be both input and output\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: w, d, create, eliminate

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2lh

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L2098
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L871-L880
";

