// File: classcasadi_1_1Function.xml
%feature("docstring") casadi::Function "

Function object.

A Function instance is a general multiple-input, multiple-output function
where each input and output can be a sparse matrix. For an introduction to
this class, see the CasADi user guide.Function is a reference counted and
immutable class; copying a class instance is very cheap and its behavior
(with some exceptions) is not affected by calling its member functions. Each
input and output has a name (name_in, name_out) and a fixed sparsity pattern
(sparsity_in, sparsity_out). The same object can be evaluated numerically
(DM arguments) or symbolically (SX or MX arguments), differentiated
(jacobian, forward, reverse, factory), transformed (map, mapaccum, fold,
expand), code-generated (generate), serialized (serialize, save) and
inspected (print_dimensions, stats, info).

Instances are created from expressions (the SX and MX constructors), from a
C body (jit), by combining other functions (conditional, if_else, map,
mapaccum) or by the solver constructors nlpsol, qpsol, rootfinder,
integrator, external. Printing shows the signature and the class name, e.g.
f:(x,y[2])->(r[2],s) SXFunction.

The exceptions to immutability are options changed with change_option and
the cache of derivative functions.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\", 2)
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, y], [x*y, sin(x)], [\"x\", \"y\"], [\"r\", \"s\"])
  >>> f
  Function(f:(x,y[2])->(r[2],s) SXFunction)
  >>> r, s = f(2, [3, 4])
  >>> r, s
  (DM([6, 8]), DM(0.909297))
  >>> f(x=2, y=[3, 4])
  {'r': DM([6, 8]), 's': DM(0.909297)}
  >>> z = MX.sym(\"z\")
  >>> f(z, [3, 4])
  (MX(f(z, [3, 4]){0}), MX(f(z, [3, 4]){1}))
  





Authors: Joel Andersson

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1uw

