%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::sparsity_in "

Get the sparsity pattern of an input, by index or name.

Numerical arguments are projected onto this pattern before evaluation:
entries outside it are dropped silently. Symbolic inputs keep the pattern of
the expression passed to the constructor.



::

  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [SX.sym(\"D\", Sparsity.diag(2))], [SX(0)], [\"D\"], [\"r\"])
  >>> f.sparsity_in(0)
  Sparsity(2x2,2nz)
  >>> f.sparsity_in(\"D\").is_diag()
  True
  >>> f.sparsity_out(0)
  Sparsity(1x1)
  





