%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::is_diff_in "

Check which inputs or outputs are marked differentiable.

All true by default; set with options \"is_diff_in\" and \"is_diff_out\". A
non-differentiable input or output is skipped by jacobian, forward, reverse
and factory: the corresponding derivative blocks are all-zero sparse. The
signature printout marks them with a '#'. Without argument, the list for all
inputs or outputs is returned.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); n = SX.sym(\"n\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, n], [x*n], [\"x\", \"n\"], [\"r\"], {\"is_diff_in\": [True, False]})
  >>> f
  Function(f:(x,#n)->(r) SXFunction)
  >>> f.is_diff_in(), f.is_diff_in(1), f.is_diff_out()
  ([True, False], False, [True])
  >>> f.jacobian()
  Function(jac_f:(x,#n,out_r[1x1,0nz])->(jac_r_x,#jac_r_n[1x1,0nz]) SXFunction)
  





See also: jacobian

