%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::mapaccum "

Create a function that applies this function N times, feeding outputs back.

as inputs

The first ``n_accum`` inputs are accumulators: in every step they take the
value of the first ``n_accum`` outputs of the previous step. For a step
f:(x, u)->(x_next, y) the result is F:(x0, U)->(X, Y) with U = horzcat(u0,
..., u_(N-1)), X = horzcat(x1, ..., x_N), Y = horzcat(y0, ..., y_(N-1)) and
x_(k+1), y_k = f(x_k, u_k). Non-accumulated inputs and all outputs are
stacked horizontally over the N steps; the accumulator inputs keep their
original shape. An accumulator output may be wider than its input (e.g.
1-by-2 feeding a 1-by-1 input): only the last columns are fed back.

Compared with writing the loop in the host language the construction is much
faster and the graph is a tower of nested unrolled loops of at most ``base``
iterations (option \"base\", default 10; -1 unrolls completely). This keeps
memory use proportional to base rather than N at a small evaluation cost.

The overloads differ in how accumulators are selected: a count ``n_accum``
(default 1), or explicit index/name lists ``accum_in`` and ``accum_out`` of
equal length that may pick arbitrary inputs and outputs. The unnamed
overload names the result \"mapaccum_\" + name(). fold is mapaccum returning
only the final accumulator state.



Parameters:
    name: Name of the result
    N: Number of steps, must be positive
    n_accum: Number of leading inputs/outputs that are accumulated; at most min(n_in, n_out)
    opts: \"base\" plus options for the resulting MXFunction



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); u = SX.sym(\"u\")
  >>> step = Function(\"step\", [x, u], [x + u, x*u], [\"x\", \"u\"], [\"x_next\", \"y\"])
  >>> F = step.mapaccum(3)
  >>> F
  Function(mapaccum_step:(x,u[1x3])->(x_next[1x3],y[1x3]) MXFunction)
  >>> F(1, DM([[1, 2, 3]]))
  (DM([[2, 4, 7]]), DM([[1, 4, 12]]))
  >>> step.mapaccum(\"F\", 3, [\"x\"], [\"x_next\"])
  Function(F:(x,u[1x3])->(x_next[1x3],y[1x3]) MXFunction)
  >>> step.fold(3)
  Function(fold_step:(x,u[1x3])->(x_next,y[1x3]) MXFunction)
  >>> step.fold(3)(1, DM([[1, 2, 3]]))
  (DM(7), DM([[1, 4, 12]]))
  >>> try:
  ...   step.mapaccum(0)
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"mapaccum: N must be positive\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: map, fold

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1wi

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L1969
