%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::generate_in "

Write or read a text file with the nonzeros of all inputs.

With arguments, writes the nonzeros of ``arg`` (one value per line, in input
order) to ``fname``; this is the input format read by code generated with
option \"main\". Without arguments, reads such a file back into a list of DM
with the input sparsities. The arguments follow the shape rules of call
(scalars are broadcast); a file with the wrong number of values raises a
dimension error.



::

  >>> import os
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"y\", 2)], [SX(0)])
  >>> f.generate_in(\"f_in.txt\", [1, [2, 3]])
  >>> open(\"f_in.txt\").read().split()
  ['1.0000000000000000e+00', '2.0000000000000000e+00', '3.0000000000000000e+00']
  >>> f.generate_in(\"f_in.txt\")
  [DM(1), DM([2, 3])]
  >>> os.remove(\"f_in.txt\")
  





