%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::serialize "

Serialize to a string that deserialize turns back into an equal function.

Any Function can be serialized, including solvers and functions with
embedded calls; a just-in-time compiled function is stored according to
option \"jit_serialize\". The string is binary-safe text; it is also what
the Python pickle protocol and MATLAB save use.



Parameters:
    opts: \"debug\" (bool) adds consistency markers to the stream



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [sin(x)], [\"x\"], [\"y\"])
  >>> s = f.serialize()
  >>> g = Function.deserialize(s)
  >>> g, g(1)
  (Function(f:(x)->(y) SXFunction), DM(0.841471))
  





See also: deserialize, save, load

