%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::factory "

Build a function computing derivatives by naming inputs and outputs.

Only defined for SXFunction and MXFunction (other classes raise an error).
The new function takes the inputs listed in ``s_in`` and returns the outputs
listed in ``s_out``, in that order. Each entry is either an existing name or
a derivative request built from existing names with ':' separators:

- inputs: \"fwd:x\" a forward seed for input x, \"adj:r\" an adjoint seed for output r, \"lam:r\" a multiplier for output r (used by ``aux``)
- outputs: \"fwd:r\" forward sensitivity, \"adj:x\" adjoint sensitivity, \"jac:r:x\" the Jacobian of r with respect to x, \"grad:r:x\" its gradient (r must be scalar), \"hess:r:x:y\" the Hessian of scalar r with respect to x and y
- an output may be prefixed with \"triu:\", \"tril:\" or \"sym:\" to return only the upper or lower triangle of a Hessian, or to symmetrize it



The output names of the result have ':' replaced by '_' (jac:r:x becomes
jac_r_x). Non-differentiable inputs and outputs (is_diff_in/is_diff_out)
give all-zero blocks. An input that is needed by an output but not listed in
``s_in`` is treated as zero. An unknown name raises an error listing the
available names.



Parameters:
    name: Name of the new function
    s_in: Input requests, see above
    s_out: Output requests, see above
    aux: Extra scalar outputs defined as linear combinations: {\"gamma\": [\"f\", \"g\"]} defines gamma = lam_f'*f + lam_g'*g, so that \"grad:gamma:x\" and \"hess:gamma:x:x\" are the Lagrangian gradient and Hessian with inputs \"lam:f\" and \"lam:g\"
    opts: \"helper_options\" and \"final_options\" (dicts for the intermediate and the returned function) and any Function option for the result



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\", 2); p = SX.sym(\"p\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, p], [p*dot(x, x), x[0]*x[1]], [\"x\", \"p\"], [\"f\", \"g\"])
  >>> g = f.factory(\"g\", [\"x\", \"p\"], [\"jac:f:x\", \"hess:f:x:x\", \"jac:g:x\"])
  >>> g
  Function(g:(x[2],p)->(jac_f_x[1x2],hess_f_x_x[2x2,2nz],jac_g_x[1x2]) SXFunction)
  >>> g([1, 2], 3)
  (DM([[6, 12]]), DM(
  [[6, 00],
   [00, 6]]), DM([[2, 1]]))
  >>> L = f.factory(\"L\", [\"x\", \"p\", \"lam:f\", \"lam:g\"], [\"grad:gamma:x\"],
  ...               {\"gamma\": [\"f\", \"g\"]})
  >>> L, L([1, 2], 3, 1, 2)
  (Function(L:(x[2],p,lam_f,lam_g)->(grad_gamma_x[2]) SXFunction), DM([10, 14]))
  >>> h = f.factory(\"h\", [\"x\", \"p\", \"fwd:x\", \"fwd:p\"], [\"fwd:f\"])
  >>> h([1, 2], 3, [1, 0], 0)
  DM(6)
  >>> try:
  ...   f.factory(\"bad\", [\"x\"], [\"jac:q:x\"])
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print('Cannot process \"q\" as output. Available: f,g.' in str(e))
  True
  





See also: jacobian, forward, reverse, which_depends

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mi

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L1213
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L2009-L2020
";

