%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::forward "

Get a function computing ``nfwd`` forward directional derivatives.

The result is named fwd<nfwd>_<name> and has n_in + n_out + n_in inputs: the
original inputs, the original outputs (out_<name>, read only when
uses_output() is true) and the forward seeds fwd_<input>, each with nfwd
times the columns of the input. Its n_out outputs fwd_<output> are the
forward sensitivities, nfwd stacked horizontally. Uses the class' own
forward mode when available (\"enable_forward\"), finite differences when
\"enable_fd\" is set, or otherwise the full Jacobian; raises \"Derivatives
cannot be calculated\" when none applies. Results are cached while alive.
``nfwd`` must be positive.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\", 2)
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, y], [x*y, sin(x)], [\"x\", \"y\"], [\"r\", \"s\"])
  >>> F = f.forward(1)
  >>> print(F)
  fwd1_f:(x,y[2],out_r[2x1,0nz],out_s[1x1,0nz],fwd_x,fwd_y[2])->(...) SXFunction
  >>> F(1, [2, 3], 0, 0, 1, [0, 0])
  (DM([2, 3]), DM(0.540302))
  >>> print(f.forward(2))
  fwd2_f:(x,y[2],out_r[2x1,0nz],out_s[1x1,0nz],fwd_x[1x2],fwd_y[2x2])->(...) SXFunction
  





See also: reverse, jacobian, factory

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1wq

