%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::stats "

Get the statistics recorded by the last numerical evaluation.

The content depends on the class: solvers report e.g. \"success\",
\"return_status\", \"iter_count\"; with option \"record_time\" every
function reports \"t_wall_total\", \"t_proc_total\" and \"n_call_total\".
Raises an error when the function has not been evaluated numerically yet.



Parameters:
    mem: Memory object (from checkout) whose statistics to return; 0 is the memory used by ordinary calls



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [x**2], {\"record_time\": True})
  >>> try:
  ...   f.stats()
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"first evaluate it numerically\" in str(e))
  True
  >>> r = f(2)
  >>> sorted(f.stats().keys())
  ['n_call_total', 't_proc_total', 't_wall_total']
  





See also: checkout

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mj

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L2788
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L1080-L1090
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::has_free "

Check whether the outputs contain symbols that are not inputs.

Only possible for SXFunction and MXFunction constructed with \"allow_free\".
Such a function can be called symbolically but not numerically, expanded,
code-generated or differentiated into a numerically usable form.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); p = SX.sym(\"p\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [x*p], {\"allow_free\": True})
  >>> f.has_free(), f.get_free(), f.free_sx()
  (True, ['p'], [SX(p)])
  >>> try:
  ...   f(1)
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"since variables [p] are free\" in str(e))
  True
  >>> f(SX.sym(\"q\"))
  SX((q*p))
  >>> Function(\"g\", [x], [x]).has_free()
  False
  





