%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::n_instructions "

Get the number of instructions of the algorithm (SXFunction and MXFunction)

The algorithm is the sequence of operations evaluated for a call, including
the input and output instructions; instruction_id, instruction_input,
instruction_output, instruction_constant and instruction_MX inspect them by
index. Other classes raise.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, y], [x*y + 1])
  >>> f.n_instructions()
  6
  >>> for k in range(f.n_instructions()):
  ...   print(f.instruction_id(k), f.instruction_input(k), f.instruction_output(k))
  45 [0, 0] [0]
  45 [1, 0] [1]
  3 [0, 1] [0]
  44 [] [1]
  1 [0, 1] [0]
  46 [0] [0, 0]
  >>> f.instruction_id(3) == OP_CONST, f.instruction_constant(3)
  (True, 1.0)
  





See also: instruction_id, instructions_sx, n_nodes

