%feature("docstring") casadi::Function::find_functions "

Get all functions embedded in this function, recursively.

Walks the owned functions (get_function) and their owned functions in turn,
returning each distinct Function once, in depth-first discovery order.



Parameters:
    max_depth: Maximum nesting depth to descend; 0 returns only the directly owned functions, a negative number means no limit



Returns:
    Unique list of embedded functions



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> inner = Function(\"inner\", [x], [sin(x)]).expand()
  >>> middle = Function(\"middle\", [x], [inner(x) + 1])
  >>> outer = Function(\"outer\", [x], [middle.call([x], False, True)[0]*2])
  >>> [g.name() for g in outer.find_functions()]
  ['middle', 'inner']
  >>> [g.name() for g in outer.find_functions(0)]
  ['middle']
  >>> outer.find_function(\"inner\")
  Function(inner:(i0)->(o0) SXFunction)
  >>> Function(\"o2\", [x], [middle(x)*2]).get_function()
  ['inner']
  





See also: find_function, get_function

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1y6

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L3685
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L2067-L2082
";

