%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::times "

Elementwise multiplication: (x,y) -> x .* y.

Elementwise (Hadamard) product, not the matrix product; use mtimes for that.
Shape rules as for plus. The result is structurally zero wherever either
operand is, so the sparsity pattern is the intersection of the patterns.



::

  >>> times(DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4]))
  DM([3, 8])
  >>> DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]) * DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  DM(
  [[1, 4],
   [9, 16]])
  >>> DM.eye(2) * DM.ones(2, 2)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  





