%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::is_linear "

Is expr linear in var?

Defined as: no entry of ``expr`` depends on ``var`` with order 2 (see
which_depends). Only the structure of the graph is inspected, not the
values: false negatives are possible (an expression may not be recognised as
linear while it really is, e.g. x*x/x). Operations whose derivative is
structurally zero, such as floor, sign or comparisons, are treated as
linear. A constant expression counts as linear.



::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  * >>> is_linear(2*x + y, vertcat(x, y)), is_linear(x*y, vertcat(x, y))
  * (True, False)
  * >>> is_linear(sin(y)*x, x), is_linear(x*x/x, x)
  * (True, False)
  * 





See also: is_quadratic, linear_coeff, which_depends

