%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::contains "

Check if expression n is listed in v.

This function checks for correspondence between nodes. The detection does
not descend into the expression graph.

contains_all checks that every entry of n is listed in v, contains_any that
at least one is. For SX the entries must be scalar. Not defined for DM.

For mathematical dependency, see depends_on

See also: depends_on



::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\"); z = SX.sym(\"z\")
  * >>> e = x + y
  * >>> contains([x, y], y), contains([e], y), contains([e], e)
  * (True, False, True)
  * >>> contains([SX.sym(\"x\")], x)
  * False
  * >>> contains_all([x, y, z], [x, y]), contains_all([x, y], [x, z])
  * (True, False)
  * >>> contains_any([x, y], [x, z]), contains_any([x, y], [z])
  * (True, False)
  * >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\"); Y = MX.sym(\"Y\")
  * >>> contains([X, Y], Y), contains([X + Y], Y)
  * (True, False)
  * 



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2c8

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1991
