%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::hessian "

Hessian and (optionally) gradient.

Computes the gradient g = gradient(ex, arg) and the Hessian jacobian(g,
arg), an arg.numel()-by-arg.numel() symmetric matrix; the \"symmetric\"
option is set unless given in ``opts``. ``ex`` must be scalar. The overload
with ``output_g`` also returns the gradient; in Python and MATLAB this is
the variant that is exposed, so the result is always the pair (H, g). Not
defined for DM.



Parameters:
    opts: Options, see jacobian



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> H, g = hessian(x**2*y, vertcat(x, y))
  >>> H
  SX(@1=(2.*x),
  [[(2.*y), @1],
   [@1, 00]])
  >>> g
  SX([((2.*x)*y), sq(x)])
  





See also: gradient, jacobian, Function::hessian

