%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::transform "

Apply transformation passes to an expression.

Wraps the expression in a Function of its free symbols, applies
Function::transform and re-evaluates it on the original symbols. Each pass
is a list starting with a verb: \"simplify\" (followed by task names),
\"expand\" or \"external\"; an unknown verb raises an error. Without
``passes`` a default set of simplification passes is applied.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> transform(x*2*3)
  SX((6*x))
  





See also: simplify, Function::transform

