%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::symvar "

Get all symbolic primitives present in an expression.

Returns the symbols the expression was built from, in order of first
appearance, each once. For SX every scalar symbol is a separate entry; for
MX the entries are the symbolic matrices as created by MX.sym, even if only
part of such a matrix is used. Presence in the graph is a structural notion;
an expression like 0*x still lists x. Use depends_on for mathematical
dependency. Not defined for DM.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\"); z = SX.sym(\"z\")
  >>> symvar(vertcat(z*x, y))
  [SX(z), SX(x), SX(y)]
  >>> symvar(SX.sym(\"v\", 2)*3)
  [SX(v_0), SX(v_1)]
  >>> v = MX.sym(\"v\", 2)
  >>> symvar(v[0]*3)
  [MX(v)]
  >>> symvar(SX(3))
  []
  





See also: depends_on, contains

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bn

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L841
