%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::nullspace "

Computes the nullspace of a matrix A.

Finds Z m-by-(m-n) such that AZ = 0 with A n-by-m with m >= n (a matrix with
more rows than columns raises an error).

Assumes A is full rank. Computed with Householder reflections, dense; for MX
the SX algorithm is embedded as a function call node.

Inspired by Numerical Methods in Scientific Computing by Ake Bjorck



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> Z = nullspace(A)
  >>> Z.dim(), float(norm_1(mtimes(A, Z))) < 1e-12
  ('3x1', True)
  





See also: qr, pinv

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cb

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1606
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1606-L1608
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::polyval "

Evaluate a polynomial with coefficients p in x.

Horner evaluation of p[0]*x^(n-1) + ... + p[n-2]*x + p[n-1]: the first
coefficient belongs to the highest power, as in MATLAB's polyval. The
polynomial is applied to every structurally nonzero entry of ``x``; the
result keeps the shape and sparsity of ``x`` (structural zeros stay zero
even when p[n-1] != 0).



Parameters:
    p: Dense column vector of coefficients, at least one entry
    x: Point(s) of evaluation, any shape



::

  >>> polyval(DM([1, 2, 3]), 2)
  DM(11)
  >>> polyval(DM([1, 0, -1]), DM([0, 1, 2]))
  DM([-1, 0, 3])
  >>> polyval(SX.sym(\"p\", 3), SX.sym(\"x\"))
  SX(((((p_0*x)+p_1)*x)+p_2))
  



