%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::if_else "

Branching on MX nodes.

Ternary operator, \"cond ? if_true : if_false\"

Selects ``if_true`` where ``cond`` is nonzero and ``if_false`` elsewhere.
``cond`` may be a scalar or have the shape of the branches (elementwise
selection); a scalar branch is broadcast. By default the result is
if_else_zero(cond, if_true) + if_else_zero(!cond, if_false): both branches
are part of the expression and are evaluated, but the value of the
unselected branch is discarded, so a nan or inf there does not propagate.
With ``short_circuit`` true (MX only; ignored for SX and DM) the branches
are wrapped in functions and only the selected one is evaluated.



::

  >>> if_else(DM(1), DM(10), DM(20)), if_else(DM(0), DM(10), DM(20))
  (DM(10), DM(20))
  >>> if_else(DM([1, 0]), DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4]))
  DM([1, 4])
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> if_else(x > 0, x, -x)
  SX(@1=(0<x), ((@1?x:0)+((!@1)?(-x):0)))
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [if_else(x >= 0, sqrt(x), 0)])
  >>> f(-1)
  DM(0)
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\")
  >>> if_else(X > 0, X, -X, True)
  MX(switch((0<X), X){0})
  





See also: conditional, if_else_zero, Function::if_else

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1ci

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1855
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1855-L1858
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::conditional "

Create a switch.

If the scalar condition ``ind`` evaluates to the integer k, where
0<=k<x.size(), then x[k] is returned, otherwise ``x_default`` is returned
(also for negative or non-integer values). By default this is a chain of
if_else expressions, so all cases are evaluated. With ``short_circuit`` true
(MX only; SX raises an error) a Switch function evaluates only the selected
case.



::

  >>> conditional(DM(1), [DM(10), DM(20)], DM(-1))
  DM(20)
  >>> conditional(DM(5), [DM(10), DM(20)], DM(-1))
  DM(-1)
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\"); z = SX.sym(\"z\")
  >>> conditional(x, [y, z], 0)
  SX(@1=(x==1), ((@1?z:0)+((!@1)?((x==0)?y:0):0)))
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\"); Y = MX.sym(\"Y\")
  >>> conditional(X, [Y, 2*Y], 0, True)
  MX(switch(X, Y){0})
  





See also: if_else, Function::conditional

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cj

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1897
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1897-L1900
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::depends_on "

Check if expression depends on the argument.

The argument must be symbolic (for MX: symbolic primitives as created by
MX.sym, not elements of them).

The dependency is in a mathematical way: Does the value of the argument
affect the value of the expression? Equivalently, will the corresponding
entry of the Jacobian by a non-zero? This is decided by sparsity propagation
through the graph, so 0*x and x-x do not depend on x.

The symbol could still be present in the expression graph.

To check that kind of dependency, use contains(symvar(f),arg)



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> depends_on(x*y, x), depends_on(x*y, SX.sym(\"z\"))
  (True, False)
  >>> depends_on(0*x, x), depends_on(x - x, x), depends_on(SX(3), x)
  (False, False, False)
  >>> depends_on(vertcat(x, 3), vertcat(x, y))
  True
  >>> v = MX.sym(\"v\", 2)
  >>> depends_on(v[0], v)
  True
  





See also: which_depends, symvar, contains, jacobian_sparsity

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1ck

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1946
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1946-L1948
";

