%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::n_nodes "

Count the number of nodes in an expression graph.

The number of nodes of the Function that evaluates the expression, which for
SX includes symbols and constants and for MX also output nodes. Shared
subexpressions are counted once; identical subexpressions built separately
are counted separately (use cse to merge them). Not defined for DM.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> n_nodes(x), n_nodes(x + y), n_nodes(vertcat(x + y, x + y))
  (1, 3, 4)
  >>> n_nodes(SX(0, 1))
  0
  





See also: cse, Function::n_nodes

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mp

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3155
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3155-L3157
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::simplify "

Simplify an expression.

For SX, applies simplification passes such as constant folding and removal
of trivial operations. For MX and DM the expression is returned unchanged.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> simplify(x*2*3), simplify(x*0 + y*1)
  (SX((6*x)), SX(y))
  





See also: transform, cse

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mq

