%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::print_operator "

Get a string representation for a binary MatType, using custom arguments.

Prints the operation at the root of a scalar expression with the given
strings in place of its operands. ``xb`` must be a unary or binary operation
(a symbol or constant raises an error for SX) and ``args`` must have one
entry per operand.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> print_operator(x + y, [\"a\", \"b\"]), print_operator(sin(x), [\"a\"])
  ('(a+b)', 'sin(a)')
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\"); Y = MX.sym(\"Y\")
  >>> print_operator(vertcat(X, Y), [\"a\", \"b\"])
  'vertcat(a, b)'
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1d4

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3251
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3251-L3253
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::extract "

Introduce intermediate variables for selected nodes in a graph.

Rewrites the expressions ``ex`` so that selected intermediate results are
replaced by new symbols ``v`` with definitions ``vdef`` (ex, v and vdef are
outputs; in Python the call is extract(ex, opts) -> (ex, v, vdef)).
Substituting ``vdef`` for ``v`` in the result gives back the original
expressions. Only nodes that are physically shared in the graph are
detected: two separately constructed copies of x+y are distinct nodes (apply
cse first to merge them). Not defined for DM.

Options:

- lift_shared (bool), default true: extract nodes used more than once
- lift_calls (bool), default false: extract every Function call and its arguments (MX only; SX raises for lift_calls true or lift_shared false)
- prefix (str), default 'v_', suffix (str), default '', offset (int), default 0: naming of the new symbols





::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> e = x + y
  >>> extract([sin(e), cos(e)])
  ([SX(sin(v_0)), SX(cos(v_0))], [SX(v_0)], [SX((x+y))])
  >>> extract([sin(e), cos(e)], {\"prefix\": \"w_\", \"offset\": 3})
  ([SX(sin(w_3)), SX(cos(w_3))], [SX(w_3)], [SX((x+y))])
  >>> extract([sin(x + y), cos(x + y)])
  ([SX(sin((x+y))), SX(cos((x+y)))], [], [])
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\"); Y = MX.sym(\"Y\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [X], [sin(X)]); E = X + Y
  >>> extract([f(E)*f(E)], {\"lift_shared\": False, \"lift_calls\": True})
  ([MX((v_1*v_2))], [MX(v_0), MX(v_1), MX(v_2)], [MX((X+Y)), MX(f(v_0){0}), MX(f(v_0){0})])
  





See also: shared, cse, substitute

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1d5

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3316
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3316-L3321
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::shared "

Extract shared subexpressions from an set of expressions.

Same as extract with the options lift_shared true and lift_calls false:
every node that is used more than once is replaced by a new symbol named
``v_prefix`` + counter

- ``v_suffix``. In Python the call is shared(ex, v_prefix, v_suffix) -> (ex,
v, vdef).





::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> e = x + y
  >>> shared([sin(e)*cos(e) + e])
  ([SX(((sin(v_0)*cos(v_0))+v_0))], [SX(v_0)], [SX((x+y))])
  >>> shared([sin(e), cos(e)], \"w_\", \"_s\")
  ([SX(sin(w_0_s)), SX(cos(w_0_s))], [SX(w_0_s)], [SX((x+y))])
  





See also: extract, cse

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1d6

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3356
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3356-L3362
";


