%feature("docstring") casadi::Linsol::neig "

Number of negative eigenvalues.

Not available for all solvers (only \"ldl\"); uses the factorization of the
most recent nfact call, which must have been made with the same matrix.



::

  >>> A = DM([[-2, 0], [0, 1]])
  >>> L = Linsol(\"L\", \"ldl\", A.sparsity())
  >>> L.nfact(A)
  >>> L.neig(A)
  1
  >>> try:
  ...     Linsol(\"L\", \"qr\", A.sparsity()).neig(A)
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
