%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::sparsify "

Make a matrix sparse by turning numerical zeros into structural zeros.

Every stored entry with absolute value at most ``tol`` is dropped from the
sparsity pattern. With the default tol=0 only exact zeros are removed; SX
entries that the symbolic simplifications already reduced to the constant 0
count as zeros. Returns a new matrix; the input is unchanged.



Parameters:
    A: Matrix to compact
    tol: Absolute threshold below which an entry counts as zero



::

  >>> sparsify(DM([[1, 0], [0, 2]]))
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 2]])
  >>> A = DM([[1, 0], [1e-9, 2]])
  >>> sparsify(A).nnz(), sparsify(A, 1e-6).nnz()
  (3, 2)
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> sparsify(vertcat(x, 0, x * 0))
  SX([x, 00, 00])
  





See also: densify, has_zeros

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_191

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1537
