%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::pw_const "

Piecewise constant function of a scalar symbolic variable.

Builds an SX expression that equals val[0] for t < tval[0], val[k] for
tval[k-1] <= t < tval[k] and val[n-1] for t >= tval[n-2], with n =
val.numel(). ``tval`` must be increasing. The result is a sum of step
functions, so it is not smooth; its derivative with respect to ``t`` is zero
almost everywhere. Only defined for SX.



Parameters:
    t: Scalar SX variable (e.g. time)
    tval: Breakpoints, length n-1; a length mismatch raises an error
    val: Function value on each interval, length n



::

  >>> t = SX.sym(\"t\")
  >>> e = pw_const(t, [0, 2], [7, 1, 3])
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [t], [e])
  >>> [float(f(v)) for v in [-1, 0, 1, 2, 5]]
  [7.0, 1.0, 1.0, 3.0, 3.0]
  >>> try: pw_const(t, [0], [7, 1, 3])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: pw_lin, if_else, interpolant

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_193

