%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::taylor "

Univariate Taylor series expansion.

Expands ``ex`` around ``a`` with respect to the scalar symbol ``x`` up to
the given order: ex(a) + ex'(a)*(x-a) + ex''(a)*(x-a)^2/2! + ... +
ex^(order)(a)*(x-a)^order/order! The expansion is done entrywise for a dense
matrix ``ex``; sparse ``ex`` raises an error. ``a`` may itself be symbolic.
The two-argument form expands around 0 to first order. Only defined for SX.



Parameters:
    ex: Dense SX expression to expand
    x: Scalar SX symbol
    a: Scalar expansion point, default 0
    order: Highest power of (x-a) kept, default 1; 0 gives ex(a)



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); a = SX.sym(\"a\")
  >>> taylor(sin(x), x)
  SX(x)
  >>> taylor(sin(x), x, a, 1)
  SX((sin(a)+(cos(a)*(x-a))))
  >>> taylor(exp(x), x, 0, 3)
  SX(@1=sq(x), (((1+x)+(0.5*@1))+(0.166667*(@1*x))))
  >>> taylor(vertcat(sin(x), cos(x)), x, 0, 2)
  SX([x, (1+(-0.5*sq(x)))])
  





See also: mtaylor, linearize, linear_coeff

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_23q

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1843
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1843-L1845

