%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::mtaylor "

Multivariate Taylor series expansion with weighted degrees.

Same as mtaylor, but each variable contributes a given weight to the total
degree: with x = [x, y] and order_contributions = [1, 2] the degree of
x^n*y^m is n + 2*m. The length of ``order_contributions`` must equal the
number of entries of ``x``.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> mtaylor(sin(x + y), vertcat(x, y), vertcat(0, 0), 3, [1, 2])
  SX(((x-((sq(x)*x)/6))+y))
  





See also: taylor

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_23s

