%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::evalf "

Evaluate a constant expression numerically, returning a DM.

Works on SX and MX expressions without free symbols (including constant
results of function calls). The sparsity pattern is preserved. An expression
that still depends on a symbol raises an error, unlike the DM(SX)
constructor which yields nan.



::

  >>> evalf(SX([[1, 2], [3, 4]]) * 2)
  DM(
  [[2, 4],
   [6, 8]])
  >>> evalf(MX(DM([1, 2])) + 1)
  DM([2, 3])
  >>> try: evalf(SX.sym(\"x\"))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
