%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::qr_sparse "

Sparse direct QR factorization with Householder reflections.

Computes a compact representation of Q (Householder vectors ``V`` and
scaling factors ``beta``), the upper triangular factor ``R`` and the row and
column permutations ``prinv`` and ``pc`` that were applied, so that the
factors can be reused by qr_solve. See T. Davis: Direct Methods for Sparse
Linear Systems. Works symbolically on SX.



Parameters:
    A: Matrix to factorize
    amd: Use an approximate minimum degree column ordering to reduce fill-in



Returns:
    V, R, beta, prinv, pc (a tuple in Python)



::

  >>> A = DM([[3, 1], [4, 2]])
  >>> V, R, beta, prinv, pc = qr_sparse(A)
  >>> R
  DM(
  [[5, 2.2],
   [00, 0.4]])
  >>> qr_solve(DM([1, 2]), V, R, beta, prinv, pc)
  DM([0, 1])
  





