%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::qr "

Dense QR factorization using the modified Gram-Schmidt algorithm.

Factorizes A = Q*R with Q of the same shape as A (orthonormal columns) and R
square upper triangular. More stable than classical Gram- Schmidt, but
breaks down (nan entries, no error) when the columns of A are (nearly)
linearly dependent. A must have at least as many rows as columns. Works
symbolically on SX. See J. Demmel: Applied Numerical Linear Algebra
(algorithm 3.1). In Python and MATLAB, Q and R are returned as a tuple.



::

  >>> Q, R = qr(DM([[3, 1], [4, 2]]))
  >>> Q
  DM(
  [[0.6, -0.8],
   [0.8, 0.6]])
  >>> R
  DM(
  [[5, 2.2],
   [00, 0.4]])
  >>> mtimes(Q, R)
  DM(
  [[3, 1],
   [4, 2]])
  >>> try: qr(DM([[1, 2, 3]]))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: qr_sparse, chol, ldl

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18s

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1229
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1229-L1231

>  void casadi::Matrix::qr(const Matrix< Scalar > &A, Matrix< Scalar > &Q, Matrix< Scalar > &R)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Dense QR factorization using the modified Gram-Schmidt algorithm.

Factorizes A = Q*R with Q of the same shape as A (orthonormal columns) and R
square upper triangular. More stable than classical Gram- Schmidt, but
breaks down (nan entries, no error) when the columns of A are (nearly)
linearly dependent. A must have at least as many rows as columns. Works
symbolically on SX. See J. Demmel: Applied Numerical Linear Algebra
(algorithm 3.1). In Python and MATLAB, Q and R are returned as a tuple.



::

  >>> Q, R = qr(DM([[3, 1], [4, 2]]))
  >>> Q
  DM(
  [[0.6, -0.8],
   [0.8, 0.6]])
  >>> R
  DM(
  [[5, 2.2],
   [00, 0.4]])
  >>> mtimes(Q, R)
  DM(
  [[3, 1],
   [4, 2]])
  >>> try: qr(DM([[1, 2, 3]]))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: qr_sparse, chol, ldl

