%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::zeros "

Create a dense matrix or a matrix with specified sparsity with all entries
zero.

zeros(nrow, ncol) stores nrow*ncol numerical zeros; zeros(sp) stores a zero
at every structural nonzero of ``sp``. To get structural zeros instead,
construct from a shape, e.g. DM(2, 2).



::

  >>> DM.zeros(2, 2).nnz(), DM.zeros(Sparsity.diag(2)).nnz(), DM(2, 2).nnz()
  (4, 2, 0)
  >>> MX.zeros(2, 3)
  MX(zeros(2x3))
  





See also: ones, Sparsity

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1dh

