%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::__nonzero__ "

Truth value of a 1-by-1 matrix (Python: bool(x))

Only defined for 1-by-1 matrices; other shapes raise an error. A
structurally empty 1-by-1 matrix is false. A symbolic SX entry raises an
error unless the on-the-fly simplifications already decided its value (x==x
is true).



::

  >>> bool(DM(2)), bool(DM(0)), bool(DM(1, 1))
  (True, False, False)
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> bool(x == x)
  True
  >>> try: bool(x > 0)
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2oq

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L431
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_impl.hpp#L80-L86
";

