%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::enlarge "

Enlarge the matrix in place, moving the existing rows and columns to new
positions.

The new shape is nrow-by-ncol. ``rr`` lists, for every existing row, its
index in the enlarged matrix; ``cc`` does the same for the columns. Both
must have exactly size1() and size2() entries. All other rows and columns
are structurally zero.



Parameters:
    nrow: New number of rows
    ncol: New number of columns
    rr: New position of each existing row, length size1()
    cc: New position of each existing column, length size2()
    ind1: True for one-based indices



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  >>> A.enlarge(3, 4, [0, 2], [0, 1])
  >>> A
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 00, 00],
   [3, 4, 00, 00]])
  >>> try: A.enlarge(4, 4, [0, 1], [0, 1])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: resize, Sparsity::enlarge

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_19i

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2471
";

