%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::is_constant "

Check if every entry is a numerical constant (no symbols)

Always true for DM. For SX, true when no entry depends on a symbol; the
simplifications make x*0 and x-x constant. A false negative is possible for
expressions that are constant only in value, e.g. x - x after other
operations.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> SX([1, 2]).is_constant(), x.is_constant(), (x * 0).is_constant()
  (True, False, True)
  >>> vertcat(x, 1).is_constant(), SX.sym(\"e\", 2, 0).is_constant()
  (False, True)
  





See also: is_symbolic, evalf

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_19v

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2855
";

