%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::nnz "

Get the number of structural nonzeros.

Counts the entries present in the sparsity pattern. Entries that are stored
but numerically zero still count; structural zeros (not stored) do not. For
a dense matrix this equals numel().



::

  >>> DM.eye(3).nnz(), DM.ones(3, 3).nnz(), DM(3, 3).nnz()
  (3, 9, 0)
  >>> DM([[1, 0], [0, 2]]).nnz()
  4
  >>> MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 0).nnz()
  0
  





See also: numel, nnz_lower, nnz_upper, nnz_diag, sparsity

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1an

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L108
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3714-L3716
";

