%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::is_vector "

Check if the matrix is a row or column vector.

True when size1() or size2() is one, so scalars and n-by-1 or 1-by-n empties
count. A 0-by-0 matrix does not.



::

  >>> DM(3, 1).is_vector(), DM(1, 3).is_vector(), DM(1, 1).is_vector()
  (True, True, True)
  >>> DM(3, 3).is_vector(), DM(0, 1).is_vector(), DM(0, 0).is_vector()
  (False, True, False)
  





See also: is_row, is_column

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1b3

