%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::set_max_depth "

Set the depth to which SX subexpressions are compared during simplification.

The on-the-fly simplifications (x - x -> 0, x/x -> 1, x == x -> 1, ...)
recognise two operands as equal when they are the same node, or, up to this
depth, when they are the same operation applied to equal operands. Depth 1
(the default) recognises (x+y) - (x+y); depth 2 also sin(x+y) - sin(x+y).
Depth 0 compares nodes only. Global setting, SX only; calling without an
argument restores the default.



Parameters:
    eq_depth: Comparison depth, default 1



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> sin(x + y) - sin(x + y)
  SX((sin((x+y))-sin((x+y))))
  >>> SX.set_max_depth(2)
  >>> sin(x + y) - sin(x + y)
  SX(0)
  >>> SX.set_max_depth()
  >>> SX.get_max_depth()
  1
  





See also: get_max_depth, is_equal

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_19b

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2101
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sx_instantiator.cpp#L44-L46
";

