%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::eye "

Create an n-by-n identity matrix.

The result is sparse: only the n diagonal entries are structural nonzeros.



::

  >>> DM.eye(2)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  >>> DM.eye(3).nnz(), DM.eye(0).dim()
  (3, '0x0')
  





