%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::inv_node "

Symbolic matrix inverse node.

Creates a single node representing the inverse of the square matrix ``x``.
The node defines its derivatives (via -inv(x) dx inv(x)) but cannot be
evaluated numerically or expanded to SX; it is meant as a placeholder in
symbolic manipulations. For an inverse that can be evaluated use inv or
solve.



::

  >>> A = MX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2)
  >>> inv_node(A), inv_node(A).is_op(OP_INVERSE), jacobian(inv_node(A), A).shape
  (MX(inv(A)), True, (4, 4))
  >>> try:
  ...   inv_node(MX.sym(\"B\", 2, 3))
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"must be square\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: inv, solve

