%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::convexify "

Make a symmetric matrix positive definite at evaluation time.

Returns an expression with the sparsity pattern of ``H`` that, when
evaluated, modifies the value of ``H`` so that it is positive definite.
Intended for Hessians in SQP-type methods. ``H`` must be square and
symmetric or triangular (a triangular pattern is interpreted as one half of
a symmetric matrix); other patterns raise an error. The node has no
derivatives.



Parameters:
    H: Square expression with a symmetric or triangular sparsity pattern
    opts: Options: \"strategy\": \"eigen-clip\" (default, eigenvalues below the margin are set to the margin), \"eigen-reflect\" (their absolute value is taken) or \"regularize\" (a multiple of the identity is added; symmetric patterns only); \"margin\": smallest allowed eigenvalue, default 1e-7, must be nonnegative; \"max_iter_eig\": iteration limit of the eigenvalue computation, default 200; \"verbose\": print the block structure found. Unknown keys raise an error.



::

  >>> H = MX.sym(\"H\", 2, 2)
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [H], [convexify(H)])
  >>> f(DM([[1, 0], [0, -2]]))
  DM(
  [[1, 0],
   [0, 1e-07]])
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [H], [convexify(H, {\"strategy\": \"eigen-reflect\"})])
  >>> f(DM([[1, 0], [0, -2]]))
  DM(
  [[1, 0],
   [0, 2]])
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [H], [convexify(H, {\"strategy\": \"regularize\", \"margin\": 0.5})])
  >>> f(DM([[1, 0], [0, -2]]))
  DM(
  [[3.5, 0],
   [0, 0.5]])
  >>> try:
  ...   convexify(H, {\"strategy\": \"foo\"})
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Invalid convexify strategy\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: nlpsol

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ql

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L3086
