%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::split_primitives "

Split a value along the symbolic primitives of this expression.

Uses this expression (a valid Function input, see is_valid_input) as a
template: ``x`` must have the same shape and is cut into one piece per
primitive, each with the shape of that primitive. The typical use is to
split a solver result back into the variables it was concatenated from.
Works with numeric (DM), SX and MX values. A shape mismatch raises an error.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\", 2)
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\", 3)
  >>> X = vertcat(x, y)
  >>> X.split_primitives(DM([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]))
  [DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4, 5])]
  >>> X.split_primitives(SX.sym(\"z\", 5))
  [SX([z_0, z_1]), SX([z_2, z_3, z_4])]
  





See also: join_primitives, primitives

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_qq

