%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::join_primitives "

Join values along the symbolic primitives of this expression.

Inverse of split_primitives: ``v`` holds one value per primitive, with the
shape of that primitive, and the result has the shape of this expression. A
wrong number of pieces raises an error.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\", 2)
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\", 3)
  >>> X = vertcat(x, y)
  >>> X.join_primitives([DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4, 5])])
  DM([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])
  >>> try:
  ...   X.join_primitives([DM([1, 2])])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Wrong number of primitives\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: split_primitives, primitives

