%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::get_row "

Get the sparsity pattern. See the Sparsity class for details.

The pattern is stored in compressed column format: colind has size2()+1
entries, the nonzeros of column j are the entries colind(j) up to
colind(j+1) (exclusive), and row(el) is the row index of nonzero ``el``.
Without argument, the full vectors are returned. Out-of-range indices raise
an error.



::

  >>> x = DM(Sparsity.diag(2), [5, 6])
  >>> x.row(), x.colind()
  ([0, 1], [0, 1, 2])
  >>> x.row(1), x.colind(2)
  (1, 2)
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1b8

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L427
Implementation:
