%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::printme "

Return the expression with the side effect of printing its value with a tag.

Returns an expression equal to this one; when it is evaluated, every nonzero
is printed to standard output as \"|> b : value\", where ``b`` is a scalar
expression evaluated alongside it (an identifier for the print). Useful to
trace values inside a Function. The printing is not part of the returned
value and not seen by the doctest runner's output capture.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> e = x.printme(y)
  >>> e, e.is_op(OP_PRINTME)
  (MX(printme(x,y)), True)
  





See also: monitor, attachAssert

