%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::set_max_depth "

Set the depth to which equalities are checked for simplifications.

Global setting (default 1) used when building expressions: operations such
as x - y or x/y test whether their operands are equal up to this depth with
is_equal and simplify to 0 or 1 when they are. Depth 0 compares node
identity only; each extra level compares the operation and recurses into the
dependencies. Larger depths find more simplifications at a cost per created
node. Calling without an argument restores the default.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> MX.get_max_depth(), (x + y) - (x + y)
  (1, MX(0))
  >>> MX.set_max_depth(0)
  >>> (x + y) - (x + y)
  MX(((x+y)-(x+y)))
  >>> MX.set_max_depth()
  >>> MX.get_max_depth()
  1
  





See also: get_max_depth, is_equal

