%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::attachAssert "

Return the expression with a run-time assertion attached.

The result is equal to this expression, but when it is evaluated the scalar
expression ``y`` is evaluated too and a runtime error with ``fail_message``
is raised unless ``y`` equals 1. Useful to check preconditions inside a
Function. A non-scalar ``y`` raises an error at construction.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> e = x.attachAssert(x > 0, \"x must be positive\")
  >>> e
  MX(assertion(x, (0<x)))
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [e])
  >>> f(1)
  DM(1)
  >>> try:
  ...   f(-1)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Assertion error: x must be positive\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: monitor, printme

