%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::eval_mx "

Re-apply the operation of this node to new dependencies.

Creates the same operation as this node, applied to ``arg`` instead of the
node's own dependencies, with the usual simplifications. ``arg`` must have
exactly n_dep() entries of matching shapes; a mismatch is a developer error.
Symbolic primitives and constants return the node itself. Call nodes are re-
called with the new arguments; OutputNodes cannot be evaluated this way.
Mainly useful for writing graph transformations.



Parameters:
    arg: New dependencies
    unique: Internal hints that the arguments are not referenced elsewhere; leave empty



Returns:
    List with n_out() results



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> (x * y).eval_mx([MX(2), MX(3)]), (x + y).eval_mx([y, x])
  ([MX(6)], [MX((y+x))])
  >>> MX.sym(\"v\", 3)[1].eval_mx([MX([4, 5, 6])])
  [MX([4, 5, 6][1])]
  





See also: dep, n_dep, graph_substitute

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_rn

