%feature("docstring") casadi::Opti::set_linear_scale "

Set the linear scaling of a decision variable.

The solver works with (x-offset)/scale instead of x; all user-facing values
(value(), initial guesses, duals) stay in the original units. Useful when
variables differ by orders of magnitude.



Parameters:
    x: Decision variable or linear mapping of variables
    scale: Scalar or matrix of the shape of ``x`` (default 1)
    offset: Scalar or matrix of the shape of ``x`` (default 0)



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> T = opti.variable()
  >>> opti.set_linear_scale(T, 20, 273.15)
  >>> opti.minimize((T-300)**2)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> round(sol.value(T), 3), opti.x_linear_scale, opti.x_linear_scale_offset
  (300.0, DM(20), DM(273.15))
  >>> round(float(opti.debug.arg()[\"x0\"]), 4)
  -13.6575
  





