%feature("docstring") casadi::OptiAdvanced::minimize "

Set the objective.

The objective must be a scalar expression in the variables and parameters of
this instance; a non-scalar raises an error. The default objective is 0.
Each call replaces the previous objective. Dual variables (opti.dual,
opti.lam_g) may not appear in it.



Parameters:
    f: Scalar MX expression to minimize
    linear_scale: The solver sees f divided by this factor (default 1)



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable(2)
  >>> opti.minimize(sumsqr(x))
  >>> opti.minimize(x[0]**2, 2)
  >>> print(opti.f, opti.f_linear_scale)
  sq(opti..._x_1[0]) 2.0
  >>> try:
  ...   opti.minimize(x)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(str(e).splitlines()[-1])
  Objective must be scalar, got 2x1.
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1a

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.hpp#L348
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.cpp#L114-L120
