%feature("docstring") casadi::OptiAdvanced::value_variables "

Get assignment expressions for the latest values.

value_variables() gives value==var for every variable with its latest solver
result; value_parameters() gives value==par for every parameter with its set
value. Both feed set_initial()/set_value() to transfer a solution to the
next solve or to another Opti.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> p = opti.parameter()
  >>> opti.minimize((x-p)**2)
  >>> opti.set_value(p, 2)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> print(opti.value_variables(), opti.value_parameters())
  [MX((2==opti..._x_1))] [MX((2==opti..._p_1))]
  >>> opti.set_initial(sol.value_variables())
  >>> opti.value(x, opti.initial())
  2.0
  



