%feature("docstring") casadi::OptiAdvanced::lam_g "

Get all (scalarised) dual variables as a symbolic column vector.

One multiplier per row of g(), as the solver reports them: with Lagrangian f
+ lam_g'*g, an entry is positive when the upper bound is active and negative
when the lower bound is active, and -lam_g is the sensitivity of the optimal
objective to the active bound. Useful for the Lagrangian Hessian, warm
starting (set_initial) and as input or output of to_function(). In Python
this is a read-only property.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> p = opti.parameter()
  >>> opti.minimize(x**2)
  >>> opti.subject_to(x >= p)
  >>> opti.set_value(p, 1)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> round(sol.value(opti.lam_g), 4)
  -2.0
  >>> sol.value(hessian(opti.f + dot(opti.lam_g, opti.g), opti.x)[0])
  2.0
  





See also: dual

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1i

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.hpp#L1391
