%feature("docstring") casadi::OptiAdvanced::bounded "

Construct a double inequality.

Returns the expression (lb <= expr) <= ub, which subject_to() recognizes as
a double-bounded constraint lb <= expr <= ub when ``lb`` and ``ub`` are free
of decision variables. Identical to writing lb <= (expr <= ub) by hand;
provided because Python's chained comparison lb <= expr <= ub raises an
error for MX. A static method; the instance is not needed.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable(2)
  >>> opti.subject_to(opti.bounded(-1, x, 1))
  >>> opti.subject_to(Opti.bounded(0, x[0] + x[1], 1))
  >>> opti.ng, opti.lbg, opti.ubg
  (3, MX(vertcat(all_-1(2x1), 0)), MX(ones(3x1)))
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1k

