%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::resize "

Change the shape in place, keeping the nonzeros that still fit.

Nonzeros with row >= ``nrow`` or column >= ``ncol`` are dropped; growing
adds structural zeros. Unlike reshape, the (row, col) position of the kept
nonzeros is unchanged. The object is rebound to the new pattern; other
references to the old pattern are unaffected.



Parameters:
    nrow: New number of rows, nonnegative
    ncol: New number of columns, nonnegative



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.dense(3, 3); sp.resize(2, 2); print(sp)
  2x2
  >>> sp.resize(4, 4); print(DM(sp, 1))
  [[1, 1, 00, 00], 
   [1, 1, 00, 00], 
   [00, 00, 00, 00], 
   [00, 00, 00, 00]]
  >>> sp.resize(0, 2); print(sp)
  0x2
  





See also: enlarge, reshape

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2nu

