%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::add_nz "

Nonzero index of entry (rr, cc), inserting the entry into the pattern if
needed.

Returns the position of the entry among the nonzeros. If the entry is a
structural zero, the object is rebound to a pattern that includes it
(nonzero indices after it shift by one). Negative indices count from the
end. An index out of bounds raises an error.



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity(3, 3)
  >>> sp.add_nz(1, 1), sp.add_nz(0, 0), sp.add_nz(1, 1), sp
  (0, 0, 1, Sparsity(3x3,2nz))
  >>> DM(sp, 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00, 00],
   [00, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 00]])
  >>> try: sp.add_nz(3, 0)
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"out of bounds\")
  out of bounds
  





