%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::get_nz "

Map flat (column-major) element indices to nonzero indices.

Each entry of ``indices`` is replaced by the nonzero index of that element,
or by -1 if the element is a structural zero. Entries that are already
negative are left alone. The indices need not be sorted. For a dense pattern
the vector is returned unchanged, without range checking.



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.triplet(3, 4, [0, 2, 1, 0], [0, 0, 2, 3])
  >>> sp.get_nz([0, 2, 4, 9, 1])
  [0, 1, -1, 3, -1]
  >>> Sparsity.dense(2, 2).get_nz([3, 0])
  [3, 0]
  





