%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::erase "

Turn the entries with flat (column-major) indices ``rr`` into structural
zeros.

The shape is unchanged. Indices may be unsorted and negative; out of range
raises an error. The object is rebound to the new pattern.



Parameters:
    rr: Flat element indices, in [0, numel())
    ind1: If true, indices are one-based



Returns:
    Mapping of length nnz() of the result: nonzero k of the result was nonzero mapping[k] of the original pattern



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.dense(3, 3)
  >>> sp.erase([0, 4, 8]), sp
  ([1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7], Sparsity(3x3,6nz))
  >>> DM(sp, 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 1, 1],
   [1, 00, 1],
   [1, 1, 00]])
  >>> try: Sparsity.dense(3, 3).erase([9])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"out of range\")
