%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::is_selection "

Check whether the pattern is that of a selection matrix.

A selection matrix S picks a subset of the entries of a dense vector: S @ v
is a vector of distinct entries of v. The pattern has at most one nonzero
per column and exactly one per row. Equivalent to
is_orthonormal_rows(allow_empty).



Parameters:
    allow_empty: If true, rows without nonzeros are allowed (the result may contain structural zeros)



::

  >>> S = Sparsity.triplet(2, 3, [0, 1], [2, 0])
  >>> DM(S, 1) @ DM([10, 20, 30])
  DM([30, 10])
  >>> S.is_selection(), Sparsity.triplet(2, 3, [0], [2]).is_selection()
  (True, False)
  >>> Sparsity.triplet(2, 3, [0], [2]).is_selection(True)
  True
  >>> Sparsity.diag(3, 2).is_selection()
  False
  





See also: is_permutation, is_orthonormal_rows

