https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L3752
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.cpp#L759-L766
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::star_coloring "

Star coloring of a symmetric pattern (greedy distance-2 coloring)

Algorithm 4.1 in Gebremedhin, Manne and Pothen, What Color Is Your
Jacobian?, SIAM Rev. 47(4), 2006. Exploits symmetry so that fewer colors
than uni_coloring are needed to recover all nonzeros of a Hessian. Symmetry
is assumed, not checked; a non-square pattern raises an error.



Parameters:
    ordering: 0 for the natural column order, 1 (default) to color in largest_first() order
    cutoff: If more than this many colors are needed, a null Sparsity is returned (only honoured with ``ordering`` 0)



Returns:
    A size2() -by-ncolors pattern: column c lists the columns with color c



::

  >>> H = Sparsity.banded(4, 1)
  >>> DM(H.star_coloring(), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 1, 00],
   [1, 00, 00],
   [00, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 1]])
  >>> Sparsity.diag(5).star_coloring()
  Sparsity(5x1)
