%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::permutation "

Construct the pattern of a permutation matrix P from a permutation vector p.

P is square with one nonzero per row and column, placed such that
multiplying a column vector v from the left gives the same result as
indexing it: P @ v == v[p]. The inverse of a permutation matrix is its
transpose, so ``invert`` true returns the transpose pattern, for which P @ v
puts v[i] at position p[i].



Parameters:
    p: Permutation vector: every integer in [0, len(p)) exactly once; anything else raises an error
    invert: If true, build the inverse (transposed) permutation



::

  >>> P = Sparsity.permutation([2, 0, 1])
  >>> DM(P, 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 00, 1],
   [1, 00, 00],
   [00, 1, 00]])
  >>> DM(P, 1) @ DM([10, 20, 30])
  DM([30, 10, 20])
  >>> DM(Sparsity.permutation([2, 0, 1], True), 1) @ DM([10, 20, 30])
  DM([20, 30, 10])
  >>> Sparsity.permutation([2, 0, 1], True) == P.T
  True
  >>> try: Sparsity.permutation([0, 0, 1])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"not a permutation\")
  not a permutation
  





See also: permutation_vector, is_permutation, pmult

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_244

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L850
