%feature("docstring") casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::blocksplit "

Split a matrix into a grid of fixed-size blocks.

Every block has ``vert_incr`` rows and ``horz_incr`` columns; the blocks in
the last block row or column are smaller when the dimensions are not
multiples of the increments. Inverse of blockcat: blockcat(blocksplit(x,
vert_incr, horz_incr)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    vert_incr: Rows per block, must be positive
    horz_incr: Columns per block, must be positive



Returns:
    List of block rows, each a list of matrices of the same type as ``x``



::

  >>> x = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]])
  >>> blocksplit(x, 2, 2)
  [[DM(
  [[1, 2],
   [4, 5]]), DM([3, 6])], [DM([[7, 8]]), DM(9)]]
  >>> blockcat(blocksplit(x, 2, 2))
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 3],
   [4, 5, 6],
   [7, 8, 9]])
  





