%feature("docstring") casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::offset "

Get the block offsets of a list of matrices.

Returns the cumulative row counts (or column counts when ``vert`` is false)
of the matrices in ``v``, starting with 0. The result has one entry more
than ``v`` and is the offset list that vertsplit (or horzsplit) needs to
undo a vertcat (or horzcat) of ``v``.



Parameters:
    v: List of matrices (or Sparsity patterns)
    vert: True for row offsets, false for column offsets



Returns:
    List of offsets of length len(v)+1



::

  >>> offset([DM(2, 3), DM(4, 3)])
  [0, 2, 6]
  >>> offset([DM(2, 3), DM(2, 4)], False)
  [0, 3, 7]
  >>> offset([])
  [0]
  





See also: vertsplit, horzsplit

