in order. The last block is smaller when the column count is not a multiple
of ``incr``. A matrix without columns gives an empty list. Each block
carries the corresponding part of the sparsity pattern. Inverse of horzcat:
horzcat(horzsplit(x, incr)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    incr: Number of columns per block, must be positive



Returns:
    List of matrices of the same type as ``x``



::

  >>> horzsplit(SX.sym(\"x\", 1, 3))
  [SX(x_0), SX(x_1), SX(x_2)]
