%feature("docstring") casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::sparsity_cast "

Cast matrix nonzeros to different Sparsity.

Keeps the nonzero values of ``x`` in storage order and gives them the
pattern ``sp``, which must have the same number of nonzeros (an error is
raised otherwise). Unlike reshape, the dimensions and the positions of the
nonzeros can change freely; only the nonzero count is preserved. This is how
the nonzeros of a sparse matrix are extracted as a dense vector.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) whose nonzeros are reused
    sp: Target pattern with x.nnz() nonzeros



Returns:
    Matrix of the same type as ``x`` with pattern ``sp``



::

  >>> sparsity_cast(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), Sparsity.dense(1, 4))
  DM([[1, 3, 2, 4]])
  >>> sparsity_cast(DM.eye(3), Sparsity.dense(3, 1))
  DM([1, 1, 1])
  >>> sparsity_cast(MX.sym(\"x\", Sparsity.diag(3)), Sparsity.dense(3, 1))
  MX(nonzeros(x))
  >>> sparsity_cast(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2), Sparsity.dense(3, 1))
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
  RuntimeError: ...Mismatching nonzero count...
  





See also: reshape

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_24z

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1236
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1236-L1238
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::sprank "

Obtain the structural rank of a sparsity-pattern.

The structural rank is the size of a maximum matching between rows and
columns of the pattern (via the Dulmage-Mendelsohn decomposition): an upper
bound on the numerical rank that depends only on which entries are
structurally nonzero, not on their values. A dense matrix always has full
structural rank, even when it is numerically singular.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity); only x.sparsity() is used



Returns:
    Structural rank, at most min(size1, size2)



::

  >>> sprank(Sparsity.diag(3))
  3
  >>> sprank(Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [0, 1, 2], [0, 0, 0]))
  1
  >>> sprank(DM([[1, 2], [2, 4]]))
  2
  >>> sprank(DM(2, 3))
  0
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_43

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1273
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1273-L1275
";

