%feature("docstring") casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::kron "

Kronecker tensor product.

Creates a block matrix in which block (i, j) is a_ij*b, for any shapes of
``a`` and ``b``. The result is a.size1()*b.size1() by a.size2()*b.size2()
with the Kronecker product of the sparsity patterns.



::

  >>> kron(DM([[1, 2]]), DM([[1], [10]]))
  DM(
  [[1, 2],
   [10, 20]])
  >>> kron(DM.eye(2), DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 00, 00],
   [3, 4, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 1, 2],
   [00, 00, 3, 4]])
  >>> kron(MX.sym(\"a\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"b\", 1, 2)).shape
  (2, 4)
  



