%feature("docstring") casadi::SXElem::lt "

Logical less than: (x,y) -> x < y.

Elementwise comparison; shape rules as for plus. Every comparison in this
group returns a matrix of the same type as the operands with entries 1
(true) and 0 (false): for DM a numeric 0/1 matrix, not a boolean, and for SX
and MX a symbolic expression that is only decided at evaluation time.
Comparisons with NaN are false. The result is sparse where both operands are
structurally zero (0 < 0 is false).



::

  >>> lt(DM([1, 2, 3]), 2)
  DM([1, 0, 0])
  >>> DM([1, 2, 3]) < DM([3, 2, 1])
  DM([1, 0, 0])
  >>> SX.sym(\"x\", 2) < SX.sym(\"y\", 2)
  SX([(x_0<y_0), (x_1<y_1)])
  >>> DM.eye(2) < 1
  DM(
  [[0, 1],
   [1, 0]])
  





See also: le, gt, ge, eq, ne, if_else

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_or

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L318
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L318-L320
";

