%feature("docstring") casadi::SXElem::logic_and "

Logical ``and``

Returns (an expression evaluating to) 1 where both entries are nonzero and 0
otherwise, elementwise

Any nonzero value, including NaN, counts as true. Shape rules as for plus;
the result is structurally zero wherever either operand is. The Python
keyword ``and`` does not work on matrices (it needs a single truth value);
use this function.



::

   >>> logic_and(DM([1, 2, 0]), DM([3, 0, 0]))
   DM([1, 0, 0])
   >>> logic_and(SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"y\"))
   SX((x&&y))
   >>> logic_and(DM.eye(2), DM.ones(2, 2))
   DM(
   [[1, 00],
    [00, 1]])





See also: logic_or, logic_not

