Two argument arc tangent: (y,x) -> atan2(y,x)

theta = atan2(y,x) corresponds to x = r cos(theta), y = r sin(theta)

Angle in (-pi, pi] of the point (x, y), taking the quadrant into account;
the first argument is the y coordinate, as in C and numpy. Elementwise,
shape rules as for plus. atan2(0, 0) is 0.



