%feature("docstring") casadi::SXElem::printme "

Debug printing: (x,y) -> x, printing x when evaluated.

Identity operation with a side effect: whenever the expression is evaluated
inside a Function (and hence inside a solver), every nonzero of ``x`` is
printed on its own line as \"|> y : value\" in storage (column- major)
order, with ``y`` an identifier of choice to tell several printme nodes
apart. Available as a method x.printme(y) in Python; the derivative is that
of ``x``. Use monitor to print a whole matrix at once.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [x.printme(7) * 2])
  >>> f(3)
  |> 7 : 3.0000000000000000e+00
  DM(6)
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2on

