%feature("docstring") casadi::IndexReduction::nlpsol_out "

Get the name of an NLP solver output by index.



Parameters:
    ind: Index in 0.. nlpsol_n_out() -1; any other value gives an empty string

>Output scheme: casadi::NlpsolOutput (NLPSOL_NUM_OUT = 6)

+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+
|  Full name   | Short |                    Description                    |
+==============+=======+===================================================+
| NLPSOL_X     | x     | Decision variables at the optimal solution (nx x  |
|              |       | 1)                                                |
+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+
| NLPSOL_F     | f     | Cost function value at the optimal solution (1 x  |
|              |       | 1)                                                |
+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+
| NLPSOL_G     | g     | Constraints function at the optimal solution (ng  |
|              |       | x 1)                                              |
+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+
| NLPSOL_LAM_X | lam_x | Lagrange multipliers for bounds on X at the       |
|              |       | solution (nx x 1); negative for an active lower   |
|              |       | bound, positive for an active upper bound         |
+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+
| NLPSOL_LAM_G | lam_g | Lagrange multipliers for bounds on G at the       |
|              |       | solution (ng x 1); same sign convention.          |
+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+
| NLPSOL_LAM_P | lam_p | Lagrange multipliers for p == P at the solution   |
|              |       | (np x 1): minus the gradient of the optimal cost  |
|              |       | with respect to p                                 |
+--------------+-------+---------------------------------------------------+



::

